sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch06-05> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The mitochondria, chondriosomes and similar granules and fibrils of cells are not special entities with specific functions but clumps of heterogeneous cell contents gathered by surface tension and drawn out along the cell axis by osmotic currents arising from surface energy and adsorption, revealing a field of force and dynamical polarity in the cell.";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Chondriosomes and similar fibrils are surface-tension clumps drawn along the cell axis";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter VI, “A Note on Adsorption”; topic “Polarity and chondriosomes”. Scope: fibrillar and granular cytoplasmic structures of epithelial, gland, nerve and germ cells"
}
